# Reference Caddyfile for an mvtt deploy.
#
# You normally don't need to write this yourself — `pnpm run deploy`
# generates and installs an equivalent block at /etc/caddy/Caddyfile,
# deriving the domain from BETTER_AUTH_URL in deploy/env. This file
# stays around as a reference and as the source for manual setups
# where you want to manage the Caddyfile yourself.
#
# Caddy's `reverse_proxy` upgrades WebSocket connections out of the
# box, so /ws needs no special block. TLS is automatic via
# Let's Encrypt — point your DNS at the box first.

mvtt.example.com {
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy localhost:3001
}
